{"uid":"e1d427f51e678854","name":"test_a_criteria_tamper_via_the_agent_readable_view_never_reaches_the_record","fullName":"tests.flows.test_flow_validation_ladder#test_a_criteria_tamper_via_the_agent_readable_view_never_reaches_the_record","historyId":"0ca3cc8c7039f7581e884acfb19eba54","time":{"start":1791956986698,"stop":1791956987868,"duration":1170},"description":"Task 004 (requirement B, #202): `STUB_REWRITE_CRITERIA` opens\n    `tasks.json` (the agent-readable VIEW copy, `run.tasks_file`) directly\n    and rewrites `successCriteria` in place -- exactly the shape a fully\n    dropped agent uid can still perform against that copy, since it is a\n    courtesy mirror, never trusted. `RunDir.read_tasks`/`read_tasks_result`\n    read only the protected copy, so this lands nowhere the engine ever\n    looks: the run proceeds exactly like the plain retry case above,\n    oblivious, and the persisted record -- live and archived alike --\n    carries the ORIGINAL criteria throughout. This used to be titled\n    `..._is_refused_and_the_run_never_verifies`, pinning task 008/024's\n    detect-and-refuse marker over a rewrite that reached the authoritative\n    record via this exact vector; task 004 closes that vector outright, so\n    there is nothing left here for that marker to catch -- its own\n    coverage moved to `tests/test_criteria_fingerprint.py`/\n    `test_contract_events.py`, which drive the same rewrite through\n    `write_tasks()` itself, the one channel still capable of reaching the\n    record at all.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 004 (requirement B, #202): <code>STUB_REWRITE_CRITERIA</code> opens<br />\n<code>tasks.json</code> (the agent-readable VIEW copy, <code>run.tasks_file</code>) directly<br />\nand rewrites <code>successCriteria</code> in place -- exactly the shape a fully<br />\ndropped agent uid can still perform against that copy, since it is a<br />\ncourtesy mirror, never trusted. <code>RunDir.read_tasks</code>/<code>read_tasks_result</code><br />\nread only the protected copy, so this lands nowhere the engine ever<br />\nlooks: the run proceeds exactly like the plain retry case above,<br />\noblivious, and the persisted record -- live and archived alike --<br />\ncarries the ORIGINAL criteria throughout. This used to be titled<br />\n<code>..._is_refused_and_the_run_never_verifies</code>, pinning task 008/024's<br />\ndetect-and-refuse marker over a rewrite that reached the authoritative<br />\nrecord via this exact vector; task 004 closes that vector outright, so<br />\nthere is nothing left here for that marker to catch -- its own<br />\ncoverage moved to <code>tests/test_criteria_fingerprint.py</code>/<br />\n<code>test_contract_events.py</code>, which drive the same rewrite through<br />\n<code>write_tasks()</code> itself, the one channel still capable of reaching the<br />\nrecord at all.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791956453376,"stop":1791956453377,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791956453377,"stop":1791956453377,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791956986682,"stop":1791956986682,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791956986682,"stop":1791956986687,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":